# hookify rules (Claude Code only) — deliberately untracked.
# They are the FAST PATH for a fresh lesson, not a governance surface: their
# messages paraphrase the documentation law, which a tracked Tier-2 file may not
# do (single-definition rule), and Codex does not read them at all. A rule that
# proves itself gets promoted into scripts/audit-lint.js instead — host-neutral,
# already run by `npm run lint:docs`, already wired into pre-commit and CI.
.claude/hookify.*.local.md
